    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d271-a2">

                <pb facs="0454" n="358" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg358"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 212.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Marquis of Salisbury to
                        Mr. Hay.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-01-07"><hi rendition="#italic">January 7,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    the receipt of your excellency’s note of December 26th last expressing on behalf
                    of the United States Government their high appreciation of the numerous and
                    valuable services rendered by Mr. Wood, Her Majesty’s consul at Tabriz, to
                    American citizens resident in Persia during the last five years, and of the tact
                    and courtesy with which he has discharged his duties in relation to the American
                    legation at Teheran.</p>
                <p>I am much gratified at this testimony on the part of your excellency’s Government
                    to Mr. Wood’s zeal and ability, and I have not failed to acquaint him with the
                    contents of your excellency’s note.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Salisbury.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
